From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 16:40:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: share hardware restart with full reset

To power the chip off and on without module removal, the driver
needs parts of two other paths. Power-on uses the hardware restart of
full reset, and power-off uses the firmware power-off and DMA stop of
module removal. Firmware power-off waits until the chip acknowledges
firmware own, because power-on depends on it. With WED active, chip
interrupts reach the host only through the WED PCIe poll, and a WED
stop leaves that poll running. A poll of a chip in WFSYS reset times
out with an AER report at the root port.

Each restart attempt first stops WED and NPU and pauses the WED poll
until WED starts again, because a failed attempt leaves both running.
Each attempt restores duplicate WTBL and NPU configuration, and it
fails when any restart command times out, because MAC init ignores
its command results. Full reset programs
hardware RRO without WED, because WFSYS reset clears RRO registers on
NPU boards. It returns RRO tables to probe state first, because the
chip holds no session after that reset. Probe initializes MSDU page
lists once, so that a later RRO hardware init does not drop pages
that a DMA reset queued.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
